      "date": "2026-04-20T09:01:30.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS misses analyst expectations",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹10.07 (up from ₹0.61 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹113.4b (up 9.5% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹3.60b (up ₹3.38b from FY 2025). Profit margin: 3.2% (up from 0.2% in FY 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue was in line with analyst estimates. Earnings per share (EPS) missed analyst estimates by 13%. Revenue is forecast to grow 8.7% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, while revenues in the Basic Materials industry in India are expected to remain flat. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 54% per year but the company’s share price has fallen by 2% per year, which means it is significantly lagging earnings.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
